# V1 scope (locked)

Product: Denmark tenant/landlord laundry booking. Progressive web direction long-term; V1 is browser web. Local-first. No Azure deploy until landlord panel basics exist. Free-tier when deploy later.

## In scope

1. Re-establish local Postgres (runtime, connection string, migrations) — document setup in README if missing.
2. Finish Mongo → Postgres cutover (auth/bookings/tenants must not depend on Mongo).
3. Refresh tokens persisted in Postgres; verify cookie auth (HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite) during that work — including mobile Safari checks later when testing phone browser.
4. Book + cancel laundry slots end-to-end on Postgres.
5. No double booking: DB uniqueness/concurrency on slot + tests.
6. Tenant isolation: shared DB + tenant/building key on rows + enforced filters + integration tests. No separate-schema / RLS in V1.
7. Landlord creates tenant accounts (option A) — allowlist only; no open self-serve signup for booking users.
8. BuildingSettings foundation: slot length, max bookings per user (even if UI is minimal).
9. API + Web versioning basics (not Danish i18n yet).
10. Tests on auth + booking isolation paths.
11. Landlord panel only as far as: manage tenants + see bookings.
12. Booking + auth usable on phone browser: responsive breakpoints so core flows work on small screens (same codebase; no separate mobile app). Desktop can stay primary for landlord panel polish.

## Out of scope (V2+)

Full PWA install/offline, distinct mobile-only UI redesign, Danish i18n, notice board, slot trading, Face ID, photo fault reports, varmemester forward, CSV/PDF regnskab, App Insights/alerts, IP banlists, schema-per-tenant, RLS, cold-start ping cron, payment/Bogføringslov, native apps.

## Defaults when unsure

- Ship simplest correct isolation and invite model.
- One web codebase; layout changes via screen size (responsive), not a second app.
- Attach learning to a shippable outcome (no orphan “learn YAML” tickets).
- Update `ROADMAP.md` checkboxes when a milestone lands — do not expand V1 without Sten explicitly unlocking scope.
